.TH SDL_SetGamepadSensorEnabled 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetGamepadSensorEnabled \- Set whether data reporting for a gamepad sensor is enabled.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gamepad.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetGamepadSensorEnabled(SDL_Gamepad *gamepad, SDL_SensorType type, bool enabled);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sensors are disabled by default and this function is used to enable them\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I gamepad
the gamepad to update\[char46]
.TP
.I type
the type of sensor to enable/disable\[char46]
.TP
.I enabled
whether data reporting should be enabled\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GamepadHasSensor (3),
.BR SDL_GamepadSensorEnabled (3)
